WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.900
How are you today, Yayoi?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.230
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.780
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.060
I read another fascinating book.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.690
My, what was this fascinating book called?

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.380
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.840
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.080
Yes, gladly.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.740
It was the tale of a boy born of the hands of man.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.840
Created by a genius scientist, the mechanical child

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.840
has the power to hold two hundred tons,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.430
while flying through the sky,
or to carry a robot into space.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:47.850
But the boy's innocent, youthful antics finally irritate his scientist father...

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.560
My, what a futuristic story!

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.490
This cute young automaton had a phrase he would always say.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.410
What was it? Tell me.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.930
<i>NJAAAA-</i>

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.180
You really are a girl, aren't you, Jun?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.790
Of course. I always have been.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.790
Are you going to keep hiding it?

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.010
It's too late to tell everyone.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.050
I'd be too embarrassed to come here anymore.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:51.560
That's not true. Nobody would make fun of you.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.430
Yo.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.540
What's spooking you, Kamigamo? You sound like a girl.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.470
Don't open the door!

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.670
I'm still changing.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.310
Kaya-san's in there with you.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.730
You're such a girly man.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.360
Or are you that embarrassed for me to see your weak, tiny body?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.520
I think somebody might.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.390
Anyway, Kaya-san, please keep this a secret.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.380
All right.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.760
What are you doing, Hajime-chan?

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.250
Master
Do What You Like

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:38.990
Hey.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.230
Go pick up some things for me.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:44.230
<i>Super sale on watermelons! 500 yen each!</i>

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.790
There's a big sale on watermelons at the shopping district.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.700
I'm going to use them for a special menu,
so bring all you can.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.620
Sure. Let's go, Kamigamo.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.480
Me, too?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.860
We men have to be the ones to do it.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.990
You wanna make Arashi-san and Kaya-san do heavy lifting?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.760
Yasaka, wait. Let me rest a bit.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.470
What? We've barely walked at all.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.730
But these are heavy.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.010
Oh, all right.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.410
Give me one.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.940
Thanks.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.260
It's pretty heavy five at a time.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.500
We're taking a shortcut.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.400
A shortcut?

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.380
I'm amazed you know about this place.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.920
Arashi-san and I go all over this area,

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.030
now and in the past.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.480
I see.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.460
I didn't know there was a shrine here.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:47.680
This place wasn't bombed, so it hasn't changed a bit.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.970
It's too hot... I'm dying.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.710
I can't go on. I can't go on...

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.620
And I'm parched.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.150
We're saved!

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.120
My wallet's with my clothes.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.100
Same here.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.790
All I have left is this change.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.190
Milk

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.740
What's wrong, Master?

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:18.570
This milk's expired.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:21.280
June 1... That was two months ago.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.350
It doesn't even feel like liquid anymore.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.380
We should throw it out.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.890
We haven't even opened it.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.130
What a waste.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.270
But you can't possibly drink it now.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.890
Any customers here with strong stomachs?

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.890
They'll shut you down.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:43.270
I know! You guys can go to the past, right?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:43.760
Yeah.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:44.410
I guess so.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.150
Then take this back to May, would you?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:57.640
If it expires June 1, the "me" existing in May should be able to drink it.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.170
It's already spoiled. I don't think it'll help to take it into the past.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.630
But it'll be before the expiration date.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.230
Oh, I get it. So it'll be fine.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.880
No, it won't!

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:10.890
Why?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.070
It won't have expired.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.510
That's just what the label says.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.520
So you're saying the label is wrong, then?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:23.200
No. What makes it wrong is that you're taking it to the past...

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.650
What's wrong with drinking milk, which expires on June 1, in the middle of May?

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.270
That's true.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.830
It is not!

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.150
Then what's wrong?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.750
You can't drink this now, right?

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.990
Of course not. It expired.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.400
And you're taking it two months into the past, right?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.550
Yes, so it won't have expired yet.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.050
<i>How do I explain this?!</i>

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.860
You drink first.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:08.610
Man, that's good stuff.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.240
What's wrong?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.590
Nothing. It's nothing.

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:16.600
I'm fine.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.220
What, you done already?

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:20.550
Yeah.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.590
OK.

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.380
You do want more.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.100
Drink.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.700
I'm fine. I don't want it.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.830
Come on, take it.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.210
I said, I don't want it.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.890
Watch out!

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.750
Ow...

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:00.780
Ow...

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.660
Be careful, Kamigamo.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:07.150
It's your fault for forcing it on me after I said I didn't need it.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.800
Why do you have my face?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.840
I ask the same of you: Why do you have my face?

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.810
I've always had this face.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.670
That's my face! Idiot!

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.150
You're a fake me!

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:24.080
You're pretending to be human and plotting to take over the Earth, aren't you?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.510
Where'd that come from?

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:31.300
Wh-What the hell?

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.110
What happened?

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.000
You're me, and I'm you.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.350
I'm you, and you're me?

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.800
You switched?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.090
That's right, Arashi-san!

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:51.480
Kamigamo is in my body,
and I, Yasaka Hajime, am in his.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.850
Oh, I get it!

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.360
I may not look it, but I'm pretty strict about money.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.140
Get your ass to work.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.010
What's that?

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:06.280
The master took over my body.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:07.460
Just like her, huh?

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.280
That's how you think I am?

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.680
I'm not imitating anybody.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.680
We really switched, Arashi-san!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.460
OK, OK. I understand.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.670
Kaya-san!

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:20.950
Yes.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.390
I may not look it, but I'm pretty strict about money.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.550
Get your ass to work.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:29.960
I'm going to murder you all.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.620
No, really...

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.610
Why won't you believe us?

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.990
I don't care if you have fun, but if it affects your work, it comes out of your pay.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.340
Anyway, the receipt and change.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.980
Arashi-san's read on her was right.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.280
What's wrong? You won't eat?

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.780
I'm not hungry.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.900
Eat!

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.500
I want my body to stay healthy.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.410
Anyhow, this body's so weak.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.130
I can't carry anything heavy,
I get tired after running just a little bit,

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.360
and I get full after barely eating anything.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.790
I'm not a glutton like you.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:15.700
I got it. The problem is that this body has a tiny stomach.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.010
I just have to enlarge it, so I can eat more, and then I'll get some stamina.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.860
Hand that to me.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:24.740
Stop it!

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:26.380
If you eat that much, you'll get fat!

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.680
But you really should gain weight.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:28.930
No! Don't eat any more!

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:30.190
Oh, come on!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.720
It's for your own good.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.640
Nobody's asking you! Stop eating and give that to me!

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.410
What are you doing?

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.370
Arashi-san?

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.740
Don't take Jun-kun's food, Hajime-chan.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:46.660
Th-That's not it. He's trying to make me gain weight...

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.690
You ate your own already.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.090
You really are such a boy.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.670
Give it back to Jun-kun.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.730
Salt, please.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.310
Fine.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.280
Good. Be friends.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.470
What are you doing, Kamigamo?

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.250
Arashi-san thinks less of me now!

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.540
It's because you're screwing around.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.430
Oh, honestly.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.810
Where are you going?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:07.930
Gotta pee.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:12.260
What?

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.810
Hey, Yasaka.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:16.470
You and I are best friends, right?

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.380
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.400
You and I are best friends, right?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.940
Y-Yeah.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.810
Then as your best friend, I have a request.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:25.470
What is it?

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.630
Don't go to the bathroom.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.570
This is something only you can do for me, and it's really important.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:33.950
Understand?

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.210
Come on. It's impossible.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.460
I have to go, or I'll pee my pants!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.210
Hold it in.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.220
No way!

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:40.860
Move!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.480
Coward.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:43.610
You're a man, right?

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.200
Being a man doesn't mean you can hold it forever.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.730
Are you breaking your promise?

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.370
I haven't promised anything yet!

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:52.140
As a man, aren't you embarrassed to betray your best friend?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.940
No best friend would ever keep me from the toilet!

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.320
Wait, Yasaka!

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:04.320
They're gone. They're gone! <i>They're gone!</i>

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.550
Dude, your body's messed up!

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:08.960
Your balls are gone!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.070
Oh man, maybe you dropped them somewhere when we switched bodies?

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.060
Don't cry, Kamigamo.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.840
We'll find them.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:23.100
That's weird. Maybe you dropped them around the shrine?

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.080
Hey, Kamigamo?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.980
Is my body OK?

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:30.960
It's not missing them, too...

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.450
I think you're OK.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.480
Show me.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.240
I want to see if my balls are safe.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.160
No!

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:38.850
Why?

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.480
I don't want to see them,

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.050
and I don't want anyone else to!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:43.590
Come on. They're mine anyway!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.530
That's not the issue!

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.770
Yes, it is!

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:49.830
Anyhow, they should be safe, so don't worry.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.620
Relax!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.960
What if they changed shape or something?

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.910
I have to see to make sure!

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:56.250
They're fine.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.700
I guarantee it.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.930
No way. Show me!

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.600
No. No. Stop.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:02.720
Please!

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.680
<i>No!</i>

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.770
Pass the salt.

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:10.800
Um, I dunno how to say this...

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.900
Do it quietly, somewhere.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:15.920
Have fun.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:18.160
She totally misunderstood that!

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.750
What do you mean, she misunderstood that?

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:20.980
You don't have to understand.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.410
Oh, no. I hadn't gone to the bathroom yet.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.900
Damn it!

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:46.050
Hey, you.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:46.690
Yes?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.450
Can I get some salt?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:49.880
Sure.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.010
You're crazy.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.170
I almost wet myself.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.690
There was no other way.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.950
Are you going to punch me every time I go to the bathroom?

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.600
So, what do we do now?

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.030
There are three possibilities.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.220
One! We wait for ourselves to turn back.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:15.550
Two! I live as Kamigamo Jun,
and you live as Yasaka Hajime.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:20.050
Three! Just like until now,
I live as me, and you live as you.

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.050
How?

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:27.710
Like a man. I'll convince everyone I'm Yasaka Hajime, and you convince everyone you're Kamigamo Jun.

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:30.150
No one will believe that.

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:31.730
Just say your voice changed.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:34.130
Your voice changing doesn't mean your face changes, too!

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:35.840
You don't know that for sure.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:37.370
Sure, I do!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.140
Then what's your idea?

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.050
It's pointless... I'm out of ideas.

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:45.470
You're fine. You just got a different body.

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:49.450
I'm missing my important manly parts!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.940
Damn, it's like I'm a woman!

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:56.370
Maybe it's my imagination, but I think my breasts are bigger, too.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.960
Feels awful.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:58.980
Stop it!

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.580
Don't touch them!

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.200
I'm just kidding... Just kidding...

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.650
They're not any bigger at all.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:08.330
Totally flat. Totally flat. Totally flat...

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.840
Mt. Fuji

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.850
Anyhow, let's think hypothetically.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.300
Hypothetically?

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.170
Hypothetically, if we do switch back someday,

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:24.050
if we each go off alone, it will be really hard to convince people when we revert.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.540
That's true.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:29.220
Please, don't do anything weird while in my body.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:34.090
At the same time, hypothetically, if we never turn back,

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:36.930
and if we start acting according to personality,

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.610
we'll seem different to others, which won't be good.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:42.790
But we are different.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:48.000
The point is this: we pretend to be who we appear.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:53.550
I'll pretend to be Kamigamo Jun,
and you pretend to be Yasaka Hajime.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.560
For how long?

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.990
Till we turn back.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:57.830
If we don't turn back, forever.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:00.840
No way. I don't wanna...

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.720
Kamigamo...

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:06.660
I can't believe I have to spend the rest of my life as Yasaka Hajime...

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.990
This sucks.

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:09.140
It just sucks!

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:12.460
Why does this have to happen to me?

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:14.810
That kind of pisses me off.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:19.530
Anyway, we may switch back real soon.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:22.690
There's no point in bitching about things we don't understand.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.570
Yasaka...

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.150
Keep your spirits up!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.910
You sure are optimistic.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:30.450
Yeah, a man's always gotta be optimistic.

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.420
Even though I'm missing my balls!

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.760
How about some cold water?

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.870
Wow, you're really serious today.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.620
I'm always serious, Arashi-san.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.110
Rice curry at table 3.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.900
Roger. I'm totally Kamigamo, dood.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.260
2 Kusuka chips at table 5.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.850
Right, Arashi-san.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:54.820
I'm totally Kamigamo, dood.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.680
Hey, can I get some salt?

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:03.580
We're low on beans. Jun, grind some more, would you?

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.120
Right! 'Cause I'm Kamigamo, dood.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.840
What are you doing? I'm Kamigamo, dood!

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.920
What's with the "dood" crap?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.670
We're pretending to be each other, right?

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.420
I don't talk like that!

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.490
I'm trying my best!

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:21.800
Stop trying to do all the little things,
and just act normally.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:22.420
Jun.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.250
Yes?

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.480
Jeez, I think you're in a glass house here.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.090
Nobody's perfect!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:31.340
Don't talk to me. Go make that order.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.430
Sorry. I'm Kamigamo, dood.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:35.990
Stop doing that!

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.490
What am I gonna do if everyone thinks I'm a weirdo...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.870
What's wrong?

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.000
Nothing. It's nothing.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.690
Kaya-san knows I'm a girl.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:50.010
If she talks to Yasaka while thinking he's me...

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.490
Kitchen

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.910
What did you want to talk about, Hajime?

00:17:53.910 --> 00:18:00.720
Um, Kaya-san, about that secret of Kamigamo's you're keeping...

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.230
Do you know his secret?

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.700
No, not a thing!

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.110
I know nothing!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.290
I see...

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:14.540
Actually, I'd like you not to talk to Kamigamo about that secret of his that I don't know about.

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:20.570
I mean, he knows. But I don't think he wants to hear it again.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.740
You should keep it a secret from him.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.440
What are you talking about?

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:30.590
Um, you see... I have no idea what I'm talking about anymore.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:33.850
What's wrong, Yasaka?

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.380
I'm Kamigamo, dood.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.850
It's no good. He's going to find out.

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:41.820
Hajime-chan! Jun-kun!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.120
Go back in time?

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.590
Master says it's really been bugging her.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:50.910
Go back in time two months and drink this.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.780
She says she wants to see who's right.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.150
Oh, no. I didn't think of this.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.230
What's wrong?

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:02.110
Who knows what'll happen if we go through time now.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:06.990
Some unknown power could keep us from ever coming back.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:11.610
There's even the possibility that we'll form a paradox, and the universe will explode.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:15.400
And even if we survive drinking it, we'll be locked in the bathroom.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.250
No way. What should we do?

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.080
It can't be helped.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.090
Not at all.

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.120
At times like this,

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.050
we run!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:21.760
Wait!

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.590
Why, you...

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:28.260
Don't scream like a girl.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.820
I'm the one who's missing his balls.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.330
Stupid kids!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.690
Wait!

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.600
We'll lose her on the back roads.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:36.760
Hold on tight!

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.300
You drink first.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:49.300
OK.

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.550
Brings you back to life...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.490
Here.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.510
It's good.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.850
You drank it all!

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.130
Why not?

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:10.580
I'm thirsty.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.910
Same here!

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:12.990
Whatever...

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.470
I'll buy another.

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:17.040
If you've got money, then don't be stingy.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.710
Hey, that's my wallet!

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:19.670
When did you...

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.390
Well, it's mine now.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.780
It's my money!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.790
Even if it's yours, your body's drinking it, so it's fine.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.740
I won't feel like I drank it, though.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.900
Fine, fine.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:32.550
You should lighten up.

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:34.400
I'll give it back when we get home.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.810
You think you're going home alive?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.780
No! Run!

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.090
You won't get away!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.060
You're me...

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.300
and I'm you...

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.460
I'm me...

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.490
and I'm me?

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:05.990
To Be Continued

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:41.330
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:43.890
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:46.080
Yes, gladly.

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.520
It was the story of those who had mastered the culture and traditions of cooking.

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:58.050
Their history begins in 1899,
in Tokyo's Nihonbashi market,

00:22:58.050 --> 00:23:02.320
and continues as they move with the fish markets to land reclaimed

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:06.970
after the Great Kanto Earthquake in 1923,
passing on their traditions to ensuing generations.

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:11.680
Their obsessive focus on ingredients and the legendary taste,

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:16.560
a closely guarded secret, becomes the fuel which powers the masked heir.

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:19.700
My, what an appetizing story!

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:24.090
This prince, who so loved the world of food, had a phrase he would always say.

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:26.690
What was it? Tell me.

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:28.930
No useless-

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:32.790
When you think of a summer...

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:34.280
Gotta be watermelons!

00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:37.860
When you tap them, you can tell by their sound whether they're ripe!

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:39.470
Think this one's kinda empty.

00:23:39.470 --> 00:23:41.160
<i>That's my head!</i>

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:43.780
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.150
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.150
